   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to the\nretirement of members employed as an emergency medical technician, critical\ncare technician, advanced emergency medical technician, paramedic or\nsupervisor of such titles in a participating Suffolk county fire district",
    "basePrintNo": "S8997",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8997-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§89-ss & 603, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8997\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nthe retirement of members employed as an emergency medical technician,\ncritical care technician, advanced emergency medical technician,\nparamedic or supervisor of such titles in a participating Suffolk county\nfire district\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill amends chapter 714 of 2023 allowing Suffolk County fire\ndistricts to elect to participate in a 25-year enhanced pension plan for\nthe emergency medical service titles notated therein. The amendment\nprovides a clear mechanism for fire districts to opt into providing such\nbenefit.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subdivisions a and j of section 89-ss of the retirement and\nsocial security law, as added by chapter 714 of the laws of 2023, are\namended to provide dates of employment necessary for Suffolk County fire\ndistrict emergency medical service personnel to have the option to\nparticipate in a 25-year enhanced pension plan, and clarifies the cost\nattributed to such plan shall be paid by the fire districts who elect to\nparticipate, provided they adopt a resolution to such effect and file a\ncertified copy with the comptroller accompanied by an affidavit of the\nchief executive officer of the fire district stating the fire district\nhas received an estimate from the retirement system of the cost to\nprovide a 25-year enhanced pension option to emergency medical service\npersonnel they employ.\n\nSection 2. Subdivision v of section 603 of the retirement and social\nsecurity law, as added by chapter 714 of the laws of 2023, is amended to\nclarify the amount of time emergency medical service personnel have to\nopt into a 25-year pension plan if their fire district elects to provide\nsuch benefit.\n\nSection 3. All past service costs associated with implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the participating Suffolk Coun-\nty fire district.\n\nSection 4. Establishes the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFire EMS personnel employed by Suffolk County fire districts face phys-\nically and emotionally demanding conditions in their daily work.  The\nrisks they encounter on the job often lead to premature physical\nexhaustion and emotional strain. For these reasons, last year the state\nenacted legislation providing Suffolk County fire districts the option\nto offer an enhanced pension with a 25-year retirement option to EMS\npersonnel. This bill builds upon this effort by providing a clear proc-\ness for fire districts to opt into offering such benefits, which serves\nas a powerful incentive to attract and retain highly skilled individuals\nin the emergency medical services profession.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have been\nin full force and effect on December 8, 2023.\n",
